cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Workstation Kit: diagnostics, cleanup and session optimisation for Windows"
message: >-
  If this software is useful in your work, a citation is appreciated.
  It is asked for, not required by the licence.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Braga"
    given-names: "Henrique Faria"
    website: "https://radioterapia.ai"
repository-code: "https://github.com/radioterapia-ai/workstation-kit"
url: "https://radioterapia.ai"
abstract: >-
  A single-file PowerShell application that diagnoses, cleans and optimises the
  open Windows session on a workstation, without requiring administrator
  privilege. It closes dispensable processes, stops running scheduled tasks,
  adjusts CPU priority and compacts memory, and clears temporary files and
  caches. Nothing it does survives a restart except the files the user chose to
  delete: it uninstalls nothing, and where a permanent action would be required
  it reports a finding with the command instead. It carries protection lists for
  radiation therapy, imaging, health record, remote access, backup and security
  software, so that a workstation in clinical use is not disturbed. Not a medical
  device, and not validated for clinical use.
keywords:
  - windows
  - powershell
  - system administration
  - workstation management
  - disk cleanup
  - session optimisation
  - radiation oncology
  - clinical workstation
